# Normalize line endings so a file's bytes, and therefore its sha256, are the
# same on every host. Without this, core.autocrlf=true on the Windows dev box
# writes CRLF into the worktree on checkout, which silently changes the hash of
# the hook scripts. Those hashes are recorded in the portfolio remediation table
# to assert the hooks are byte identical across repos, so an unpinned line
# ending makes that table meaningless.
#
# Measured 2026-08-09 with "git ls-files --eol": all 30 tracked files are text
# and git considered none of them binary, so no exception was required at the
# time. The binary list below is forward looking, not measured necessary. Add to
# it before committing any asset of a new type.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF regardless: the hooks run under bash and a CR would
# ride along into the shebang line and into the checker's exit codes.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Forward looking. Nothing matching these is tracked today.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.wasm binary
